[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2593928332","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101563#issuecomment-2593928332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101563","id":2593928332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6anDSM","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-15T21:01:43Z","updated_at":"2025-01-15T21:02:03Z","body":"**UPDATE**: I've exposed `rotated_local` as well. Cleaned up the doc descriptions a bit to be consistent (just within `Basis`, didn't touch `Transform3D`).\r\n\r\nTagging @AThousandShips @kleonc","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2593928332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2593989417","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101563#issuecomment-2593989417","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101563","id":2593989417,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6anSMp","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-15T21:37:28Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T00:28:00Z","body":"Optimizations are always welcome. But we need to avoid exposing new API surface without having a reason to do so. More API surface means that we have less flexibility in future optimizations and more maintenance burden. \r\n\r\nThis is not a theoretical problem, its one we run into all the time (just today for example https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101599). \r\n\r\nTherefore, I would stick to just exposing the functions that users have expressed a need for\r\n\r\n_Edit: For clarity, I meant that we should expose `scaled_local` since there is a proposal for exposing it and at least one person needs it. We should not expose `rotated_local` until there is an established need for it_","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2593989417/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2594097743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101563#issuecomment-2594097743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101563","id":2594097743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6anspP","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-15T22:50:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-15T23:42:14Z","body":"> Optimizations are always welcome. But we need to avoid exposing new API surface without having a reason to do so. More API surface means that we have less flexibility in future optimizations and more maintenance burden.\r\n> \r\n> This is not a theoretical problem, its one we run into all the time (just today for example #101599).\r\n> \r\n> Therefore, I would stick to just exposing the functions that users have expressed a need for\r\n\r\nI understand this sentiment, and I don't doubt that it's borne of a real problem. However, I think each case must be examined individually.\r\n\r\nIf we were starting the API fresh, I may agree with you. However, there is currently a glaring asymmetry in the API. `Basis.scaled` and `Basis.rotated` are already exposed. Furthermore, `Transform3D.scaled_local` and `Transform3D.rotated_local` are also exposed. This creates an inconsistency between classes, and also favors matrix pre-multiplication over post-multiplication, which is strange.\r\n\r\nFor further reason why the current API is confusing, you can look in the proposal I linked in the original post:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11560\r\nThe `get_scale()` method returns the local scale (axis lengths), and so does \"scale\" in the inspector. Yet the only `scaled` method without any qualifier is global.\r\n\r\nAs for only responding to user-expressed needs, I will express the need as well as I can here. As a 3D user with access to a `Basis`, I want this:\r\n![local](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d350b13a-f303-4718-90b2-aec3ded3275f)\r\nInstead of this:\r\n![global](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e7261efd-cbda-47ee-841b-c13435d4266c)\r\nWithout having to do this:\r\n```\r\nvar b := basis\r\nb.x *= scale.x\r\nb.y *= scale.y\r\nb.z *= scale.z\r\nbasis = b\r\n```\r\nThis isn't just tedious for such a simple and common operation, it's also just not as fast as it would be in C++. All alternatives either require me to access other data structures or to incur more math costs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2594097743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2594201769","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101563#issuecomment-2594201769","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101563","id":2594201769,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aoGCp","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T00:24:27Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T00:24:27Z","body":"@MajorMcDoom Sorry, I was unclear, I mean that we should go ahead with exposing `scaled_local` but not `rotated_local`","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2594201769/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2594214020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101563#issuecomment-2594214020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101563","id":2594214020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aoJCE","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-16T00:36:18Z","updated_at":"2025-01-16T00:36:18Z","body":"> @MajorMcDoom Sorry, I was unclear, I mean that we should go ahead with exposing `scaled_local` but not `rotated_local`\r\n\r\n@clayjohn Gotcha, my apologies for the overreaction there. I will revert the rotation stuff, and maybe that can be separately examined in another PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2594214020/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2594261521","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101563#issuecomment-2594261521","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101563","id":2594261521,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aoUoR","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"htt